task.claim:
For each of the 7 curves of
research/endosweep_dk_exact_batch4_20261022/dk_exact.json (nums/numsp384d1,
other/Curve41417, nums/ed-510-mont, other/M-511, nums/numsp512d1,
other/E-521, arkworks/ed_on_mnt4_753), with p, t, h, n, D_K, f, s and the
factorisation as recorded there:
  p + 1 - t = h*n;
  t^2 - 4p = D_K * f^2;
  4p - t^2 = prod p_i^e_i (the factorisation certificate);
  the odd-exponent p_i multiply to s, and D_K = -s or -4*s as
    nist.exact_discriminant computes it; D_K is a discriminant;
  min_nonscalar_degree(D_K) is the recorded value, 2^L <= |D_K| < 2^(L+1)
    and min_nonscalar_degree(D_K) >= 2^(L-2);
  and, if the listed factors above 10^8 are prime, D_K is a fundamental
    discriminant.
Moreover, on all 7 curves |D_K| >= 2^385 and
min_nonscalar_degree(D_K) >= 2^383.
